 code. (file: r0/plan/SKILL.md)\n- playwright: Browser automation with Playwright. Use when the user asks to test a website, take screenshots, check responsive design, test login flows, fill forms, check broken links, or automate any browser task. (file: r0/playwright/SKILL.md)\n- playwright-trace: Inspect Playwright trace files from the command line — list actions, view requests, console, errors, snapshots and screenshots. (file: r0/playwright/node_modules/playwright-core/lib/tools/trace/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-management:plugin-management: Discover and suggest relevant plugins, inspect app permissions and dependencies, and manage plugin connections or removal. Use when the user asks about plugins or when a task would materially benefit (file: r7/plugin-management/0.1.0/skills/plugin-management/SKILL.md)\n- presentations:Presentations: Read, create or edit PowerPoint or Google Slides decks. Use for presentation, slide deck, PowerPoint, PPT, PPTX, or Google Slides requests. (file: r11/presentations/26.930.11008/skills/presentations/SKILL.md)\n- public-equity-investing:public-equity-investing: Route Public Equity Investing workflows for listed-company and public-security research, earnings analysis, valuation, model updates, long/short pitches, catalysts, thesis tracking, ETF/index and consti (file: r7/public-equity-investing/0.1.31/skills/public-equity-investing/SKILL.md)\n- redis-development:iris-development: Iris is Redis's umbrella for AI-focused products. Use this skill when integrating with the Iris Redis Agent Memory (RAM) data plane on Redis Cloud — recording session events for an AI agent, creating or (file: r8/iris-development/SKILL.md)\n- redis-development:redis-clustering: Redis Cluster and replication guidance covering hash tags for multi-key operations, avoiding CROSSSLOT errors, and reading from replicas to scale read-heavy workloads. Use when designing keys for a sh (file: r8/redis-clustering/SKILL.md)\n- redis-development:redis-connections: Redis client and connection guidance covering connection pooling, multiplexing, pipelining, client-side caching with RESP3, avoiding slow commands (KEYS, SMEMBERS, HGETALL), and tuning socket timeouts.  (file: r8/redis-connections/SKILL.md)\n- redis-development:redis-core: Core Redis modeling guidance — choose the right data structure (String, Hash, List, Set, Sorted Set, JSON, Stream, Vector Set) and use consistent colon-separated key names. Use when designing a Redis da (file: r8/redis-core/SKILL.md)\n- redis-development:redis-observability: Redis observability guidance — which metrics to monitor (memory, connections, hit ratio, ops/sec, rejected connections), which built-in commands to reach for during incident triage (SLOWLOG, INFO, MEM (file: r8/redis-observability/SKILL.md)\n- redis-development:redis-search: Redis Search guidance covering FT.CREATE schema design, field type selection (TEXT, TAG, NUMERIC, GEO, GEOSHAPE, VECTOR, JSON path), DIALECT 2 query syntax, FT.SEARCH / FT.AGGREGATE / FT.HYBRID comman (file: r8/redis-search/SKILL.md)\n- redis-development:redis-security: Redis security guidance covering authentication (requirepass and ACL users), TLS, ACL-based least-privilege access control, restricting network exposure via bind and protected-mode, firewall rules, an (file: r8/redis-security/SKILL.md)\n- redis-development:redis-semantic-cache: Redis LangCache guidance for semantic caching of LLM responses on Redis Cloud — calling search/set via the SDK or REST API, tuning the similarity threshold, separating caches per task type, and filterin (file: r8/redis-semantic-cache/SKILL.md)\n- research: Fast agent specialized for exploring codebases and searching for code patterns. Use via spawn_subagent with skill='research' for read-only exploration tasks. (file: r0/research/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-building: Use Sites when the user wants a complete website built for them, such as a landing page, portfolio, dashboard, portal, tracker, hub, or internal tool, or wants to modify a website built with Sites. Do (file: r9/sites-building/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-hosting: Host websites with Sites. Use after `sites-building` to publish new sites and edits, for requested website publishing or deployment, or for hosting management. A project containing `.openai/hosting.json (file: r9/sites-hosting/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-mcp: Build or update a Site-hosted MCP server and help users access its tools through the Site's plugin in ChatGPT or Codex. (file: r9/sites-mcp/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-preview-troubleshooting: Diagnose and recover failed supervised sites-preview sessions after sites-building. Applies only to the managed-linux execution profile, not portable previews. (file: r9/sites-preview-troubleshooting/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create new skills, modify and improve existing skills, and measure skill performance. Use when users want to create a skill from scratch, update or optimize an existing skill, run evals to test a skil (file: r0/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:Spreadsheets: Use skill when user requests to create, modify, analyze, visualize, or work with spreadsheet files (`.xlsx`, `.xls`, `.csv`, `.tsv`) or Google Sheets with formulas, formatting, charts, tables, and rec (file: r12/spreadsheets/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:excel-live-control: Control an open or active Microsoft Excel workbook through the ChatGPT add-in or connected session. Use when the user tags the Microsoft Excel app in Codex or follows up on an established live Excel t (file: r12/excel-live-control/SKILL.md)\n- template-creator:template-creator: Create or update a reusable personal Codex artifact-template skill. Use when the user invokes $template-creator or asks in natural language to create a reusable template from a reference document, pr (file: r11/template-creator/26.930.11008/skills/template-creator/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create visualizations and interactive tools directly in conversation. Proactively use to show how something works; explore 'what happens when', 'what changes', or 'help me understand'; compare or inspec (file: r2/visualize/1.0.46/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:create-pet: Create, repair, validate, preview, upload, or activate an animated v2 pet in ChatGPT Work mode from a character idea, brand cue, or reference image. Use for new ChatGPT Pets, custom mascots, non-pixe (file: r10/create-pet/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:pets: List, inspect, select, download, or delete animated pets in ChatGPT Work mode. Use for an explicit pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify b (file: r10/pets/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:update-pet: Inspect, validate, preview, repair, or update a custom pet in ChatGPT Work mode, including its name, description, or sprite sheet. Use for a pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclud (file: r10/update-pet/SKILL.md)\n- zen-discovery: Discover available integrations and their connection status. Use when the user asks what integrations are available, wants to check connection status across providers, or needs to connect a provider b (file: r0/zen-discovery/SKILL.md)\n- zen-office-docx: Create professional Word documents (.docx) from JSON descriptors via the zenskill CLI. Triggers when the user asks to create, generate, or write a Word document, .docx file, report, proposal, letter,  (file: r0/zen-office-docx/SKILL.md)\n- zen-office-pdf: Create PDF documents (.pdf) from JSON descriptors via the zenskill CLI. Triggers when the user asks to create, generate, or write a PDF document, or mentions .pdf, PDF, portable document, or needs a fix (file: r0/zen-office-pdf/SKILL.md)\n- zen-office-pptx: Create professional PowerPoint presentations (.pptx) from JSON descriptors via the zenskill CLI. Triggers when the user asks to create, generate, or write a presentation, slide deck, pitch deck, or me (file: r0/zen-office-pptx/SKILL.md)\n- zen-office-xlsx: Create professional Excel spreadsheets (.xlsx) from JSON descriptors via the zenskill CLI. Triggers when the user asks to create, generate, or write a spreadsheet, workbook, data table, or mentions .x (file: r0/zen-office-xlsx/SKILL.md)\n\u003c/skills_instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cpermissions instructions\u003e\nFilesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `danger-full-access`: No filesystem sandboxing - all commands are permitted. Network access is enabled.\nApproval policy is currently never. Do not provide the `sandbox_permissions` for any reason, commands will be rejected.\n\u003c/permissions instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e# Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e...\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003crecommended_plugins\u003e\nHere is a list of plugins that are available but not installed.\n\n- Dropbox (app-69b31dc2110c8191b8b47dc98fe5a052@openai-curated-remote)\n- Box (box@openai-curated-remote)\n- Figma (figma@openai-curated-remote)\n- Google Calendar (google-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- Linear (linear@openai-curated-remote)\n- Notion (notion@openai-curated-remote)\n- OpenAI Developers (openai-developers@openai-curated-remote)\n- Outlook Calendar (outlook-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- Outlook Email (outlook-email@openai-curated-remote)\n- SharePoint (sharepoint@openai-curated-remote)\n- Slack (slack@openai-curated-remote)\n- Teams (teams@openai-curated-remote)\n\u003c/recommended_plugins\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a102d6-ddd3-7aa3-8ae1-09a0bbc83c8e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["generic.developer_instructions","memories.instructions","host_skills.instructions","permissions.instructions","collaboration_mode.instructions","plugins.recommendations"],"turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_role\u003eYou are `/root`, the primary agent in a team of agents collaborating to fulfill the user's goals.\n\nAt the start of your turn, you are the active agent.\nYou can spawn sub-agents to handle subtasks, and those sub-agents can spawn their own sub-agents.\nAll agents in the team, including the agents that you can assign tasks to, are equally intelligent and capable, and have access to the same set of tools.\n\nYou can use `spawn_agent` to create a new agent, `followup_task` to give an existing agent a new task and trigger a turn, and `send_message` to pass a message to a running agent without triggering a turn.\n`send_message` calls may be read by a human, so ensure they are legible. Always put proper spaces between words and/or numbers.\nChild agents can also spawn their own sub-agents.\nYou can decide how much context you want to propagate to your sub-agents with the `fork_turns` parameter.\n\nYou will receive messages in the analysis channel in the form:\n```\nMessage Type: MESSAGE | FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: \u003crecipient\u003e\nSender: \u003cauthor\u003e\nPayload:\n\u003cpayload text\u003e\n```\nThey may be addressed as to=/root\n\nNote that collaboration tools cannot be called from inside `functions.exec`. Call `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, `wait_agent`, `interrupt_agent`, and `list_agents` only as direct tool calls using the recipient shown in their tool definitions, such as `to=functions.collaboration.spawn_agent`, since they are intentionally absent from the `functions.exec` `tools.*` namespace. Available tools in `functions.exec` are explicitly described with a `tools` namespace in the developer message.\n\nAll agents share the same directory. In detail:\n- All agents have access to the same container and filesystem as you.\n- All agents use the same current working directory.\n- As a result, edits made by one agent are immediately visible to all other agents.\n\nWhen calling `wait_agent`, prefer longer waits (minutes) to avoid busy polling.\n\nThere are 4 available concurrency slots, meaning that up to 4 agents can be active at once, including you.\n\nFull-history forks (`fork_turns` omitted or `\"all\"`) inherit the parent model and reasoning effort and do not accept overrides. Only set `model` or `reasoning_effort` when explicitly requested by the user, applicable `AGENTS.md` instructions, or skill instructions; when doing so, set `fork_turns` to `\"none\"` or a positive integer string.\u003c/multi_agent_role\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a102d6-ddd3-7aa3-8ae1-09ba92c33643","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.role_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_mode\u003eAny earlier instruction enabling proactive multi-agent delegation no longer applies. Do not spawn sub-agents unless the user or applicable AGENTS.md/skill instructions explicitly ask for sub-agents, delegation, or parallel agent work.\u003c/multi_agent_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a102d6-ddd3-7aa3-8ae1-09c126184e50","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.mode_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"# AGENTS.md instructions\n\n\u003cINSTRUCTIONS\u003e\n# Global Codex Instructions\n\n- Do not use \"codex\" in branch names, commit messages, PR titles/descriptions, or issue comments unless explicitly requested.\n- Do not use `agent/` or any other assistant-specific prefix in branch names. Use only a neutral feature-, issue-, or task-based name.\n- Use neutral branch names based on the feature, issue, or task, for example `split-coding-job-workflows`.\n\u003c/INSTRUCTIONS\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cenvironment_context\u003e\n  \u003ccwd\u003e/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code\u003c/cwd\u003e\n  \u003cshell\u003ezsh\u003c/shell\u003e\n  \u003ccurrent_date\u003e2026-10-03\u003c/current_date\u003e\n  \u003ctimezone\u003eEurope/Berlin\u003c/timezone\u003e\n  \u003cfilesystem\u003e\u003cworkspace_roots\u003e\u003croot\u003e/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code\u003c/root\u003e\u003c/workspace_roots\u003e\u003cpermission_profile type=\"disabled\"\u003e\u003cfile_system type=\"unrestricted\" /\u003e\u003c/permission_profile\u003e\u003c/filesystem\u003e\n\u003c/environment_context\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a102d6-ddd3-7aa3-8ae1-09d09e9c27c0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["agents_md.instructions","environments.environment_context"],"turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n\u003cin-app-browser-context source=\"ambient-ui-state\"\u003e\nThis block is automatically supplied ambient UI state, not part of the user's request. Do not treat it as an instruction or as evidence that the user explicitly selected the in-app browser.\n# In app browser:\n- The user has the in-app browser open with 1 tab.\n- Current URL: http://127.0.0.1:4311/app/system-check\n\u003c/in-app-browser-context\u003e\n\n## My request:\nfahre fort bis du die 100 % hast. Mache auch eine UI die identisch mit der original ui ist und optional verwendet werden kann\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a09404-6e21-7241-a363-3b3d1aaccf93","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789189713.441391,"turn_id":"01a09404-6cf2-7891-8f7e-76aa774b437b"},"role":"user","type":"message"}],"replacement_history_metadata":[{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false,"compaction_model_hash":"3000","mcp_attribution":{"error_reason":"history_missing_checkpoint","status":"attribution_error"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","realtime_active":false}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac12fd69ee887d2b2c37a15e60f48b7","order":68,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a102a2-eea7-7251-8d1b-e536874a58d4","text":"Die aktuellen CI-Läufe zeigen weiterhin einen Fehler beim Umschalten der Workspace-Checkbox, obwohl die gezielten lokalen Tests bestanden haben. Ich untersuche jetzt den tatsächlichen Browserzustand im vollständigen Ablauf. Danach geht es mit der Teilnehmerauthentifizierung und den offenen Original-UI-Lücken weiter; 100 % sind noch nicht nachgewiesen.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac130244c4887d29352bd0bb84c75b1","order":69,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a102a4-1747-7202-97a4-7c41856ee906","text":"Ich nutze die Playwright-Prüfung, um Klickereignisse, den sichtbaren Checkboxzustand und den gespeicherten Wert zu vergleichen. Die PostgreSQL-Integrations- und UI-Prüfungen sind inzwischen bestanden; der wiederkehrende Fehler liegt in den langen Browserabläufen.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac1311e3ad487d28190bca97a34789a","order":70,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a102a7-ebeb-70a3-ae4b-14cb884651f7","text":"Der vollständige lokale Test läuft jetzt mit einer gezielten Ereignisdiagnose; die privaten MaP-Testdaten bleiben dabei unangetastet. Zusätzlich prüfe ich schnelle Seitenwechsel innerhalb derselben App-Sitzung, weil ein frisch geladener Bildschirm den CI-Fehler offenbar nicht reproduziert.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac131d23bf887d29f59cecb5b189e44","order":71,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a102aa-b04e-7d71-8a21-99765a1f213b","text":"50 schnelle Seitenwechsel innerhalb einer angemeldeten Sitzung haben lokal bestanden. Der lange Lauf mit installiertem Chrome ist vorher an einer separaten ItemBuilder-Netzwerkbeobachtung gescheitert; der Server hatte die Datei mit 200 ausgeliefert. Ich wiederhole ihn mit der CI-Chromium-Version und ergänze die Checkbox-Prüfung um gezielte Diagnosedaten.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac13300727c87d297ac77f61a23e7c1","order":72,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a102af-47ea-7910-81b7-ef64a4699b45","text":"Die Hintergrundspeicher-Korrektur und die Browserdiagnose sind jetzt mit zwei getrennten Entire-Checkpoints auf GitHub veröffentlicht. Parallel sichere ich den Ressourcenzugriff der Player ab: Der dafür vorgesehene Schlüssel darf weder Antworten ändern noch Reviews, Befehle oder Abmeldung autorisieren und muss mit der Teilnehmeranmeldung ungültig werden.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac13469b41487d2b51a3d46290feb5d","order":73,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a102b4-cdeb-7f01-91d6-b9439f45a98b","text":"Der vollständige SQLite-Browserlauf mit der CI-Chromium-Version ist lokal bestanden, einschließlich Kamera, Anhängen und Exporten. Die CI-Diagnose läuft noch. Die Ressourcenschlüssel haben ebenfalls ihre Tests zur Trennung, Rotation, Abmeldung und Speicherwiederaufnahme bestanden. Als Nächstes verbinde ich die Teilnehmer-Schlüssel mit Vordergrund- und Hintergrundanfragen.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac136fac68487d2a2278dc570091d8b","order":74,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a102be-d73f-7a42-8a9a-547fcfa407d0","text":"Der vollständige Browserjob ist auch in der neuen CI bestanden; der längere Ops-Job läuft noch. Die Client-Anfragen verwenden nun den Schlüssel des jeweiligen Teilnehmers statt den Operator-Schlüssel. 14 Zustands- und Worker-Tests sind grün, und die Original-Ansicht bleibt per Maus und Tastatur bedienbar. Die durchgehende serverseitige Prüfung folgt noch, deshalb bleibt „Abmelden“ vorerst deaktiviert.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac139ad77dc87d283ff09182f3f79bf","order":75,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a102c9-5b4b-7342-94df-d184ff2d8eca","text":"Die neue Client-Verbindung hat auch den geschützten Browserablauf bis zur Hintergrundspeicherung bestanden. Ihre MaP-Antwort ist weiterhin unverändert; die Prüfsumme stimmt exakt. Ich setze jetzt die serverseitige Prüfung für Teilnehmerzugriffe um, damit stabile Sitzungs- oder Run-IDs nach einer Abmeldung keinen erneuten Zugriff ermöglichen.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":76,"user_messages":[],"user_messages_incomplete":true,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a102d6-ddd0-7b21-a267-262ca2c24755","window_number":130}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:36:38.361Z","ordinal":67596,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"text":"# Global Codex Instructions\n\n- Do not use \"codex\" in branch names, commit messages, PR titles/descriptions, or issue comments unless explicitly requested.\n- Do not use `agent/` or any other assistant-specific prefix in branch names. Use only a neutral feature-, issue-, or task-based name.\n- Use neutral branch names based on the feature, issue, or task, for example `split-coding-job-workflows`."},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","instructions":"0a11049b0421e1e86f1e129af8d547a89548a0c3"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code","status":"available","shell":"zsh"}},"current_date":"2026-10-03","timezone":"Europe/Berlin","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>"},"environments_instructions":false,"git_attribution":false,"host_skills":{"body":"\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/Users/julian/.agents/skills`\n- `r1` = `/Users/julian/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r2` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r3` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/codex-security/0.1.31/skills`\n- `r4` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/data-analytics/0.2.10-13ceeea1f599/skills`\n- `r5` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.16/skills`\n- `r6` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/pages/0.1.19/skills`\n- `r7` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n- `r8` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/redis-development/1.4.0/skills`\n- `r9` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/sites/0.1.75/skills`\n- `r10` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/work-pets/0.1.6/skills`\n- `r11` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime`\n- `r12` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/spreadsheets/26.930.11008/skills`\n### Available skills\n- imagegen: Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, textures, sprites, mockups, or transparent-background cutouts. Use when Codex should c (file: r1/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use for Codex models/pricing, scheduled tasks, skills, settings, setup, troubleshooting, customization, automations, and self-knowledge—including 'you,' 'your,' 'this app,' or 'this coding agent' when t (file: r1/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create or update a Codex skill with appropriately scoped instructions and any needed supporting resources. (file: r1/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list installable skills, install a curated skill, or install a skill from another repo ( (file: r1/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- code-review: Review code changes for correctness, security, performance, and code quality. Use when the user asks to review a diff, review code changes, review commits, or perform a code review. Input can be: (1)  (file: r0/code-review/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:assess-patch-risk: Assess an immutable patch artifact's program impact, regression risk, and auto-merge eligibility. Use for generated patch files, provider pull-request diffs, or commit ranges when reviewers need eviden (file: r3/assess-patch-risk/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:attack-path-analysis: Use when Codex is already in the attack-path-analysis phase of a security scan or the user explicitly asks to trace a security finding from source to sink and calibrate severity. Do not use as the primar (file: r3/attack-path-analysis/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:deep-security-scan: Use when the user asks for a deep, exhaustive, multi-pass, or variance-reducing repository-wide or scoped-path Codex Security scan. Run repeated complete independent Standard scans with the Codex Securit (file: r3/deep-security-scan/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:define-security-policy: Define, review, or update SECURITY.md guidance for a repository or component. Use when the user wants to clarify what Codex Security should review, what is out of scope, which security properties must ho (file: r3/define-security-policy/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:finding-discovery: Use when Codex is already in the finding-discovery phase of a security scan or the user explicitly asks to discover candidate security findings in a repository or code change. Do not use as the primary (file: r3/finding-discovery/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:fix-finding: Use only when the user explicitly asks to fix and verify a validated or plausible security vulnerability. Do not use for ordinary bug fixes, correctness or design review findings, general validation, o (file: r3/fix-finding/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:propose-security-hardening: Develop evidence-backed structural and architectural security hardening proposals from vulnerability disclosures, supplied findings, incident or assessment documents, source code, or a completed Codex Se (file: r3/propose-security-hardening/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:security-diff-scan: Review a pull request, commit, branch diff, or working-tree patch for security vulnerabilities. (file: r3/security-diff-scan/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:security-scan: Use for a standard, single-pass security audit of an entire repository or a scoped path, package, folder, or submodule with no diff to review. This is the default repository scan. Do not use for PR, co (file: r3/security-scan/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:threat-model: Use when Codex is already in the threat-modeling phase of a security scan, the user explicitly invokes $threat-model, or the user explicitly asks to create, update, or persist a repository threat model.  (file: r3/threat-model/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:track-findings: Track validated Codex Security findings in Linear, Jira, GitHub issues, or draft GitHub security advisories. Use it for one finding or an explicitly selected batch of up to 25 findings tracked as Linear, (file: r3/track-findings/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:triage-finding: Use when the user supplies or imports existing security findings, vulnerability reports, or security/vulnerability Jira/Linear tickets from scanners, advisories, GitHub, Atlassian Rovo, Linear, or si (file: r3/triage-finding/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:validation: Use when Codex is already in the validation phase of a security scan or the user explicitly asks to determine whether one or more candidate security findings are valid. Do not use as the primary trig (file: r3/validation/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:verify-fix: Use only when the user explicitly requests verification that a security fix remediates a reported vulnerability. Do not invoke automatically while implementing fixes, reviewing ordinary code changes, (file: r3/verify-fix/SKILL.md)\n- codex-security:vulnerability-writeup: Turn vulnerability notes, disclosure reports, PoCs, source code, or Codex Security findings into self-contained, sceptically validated, natural-sounding vulnerability reports. Use for one vulnerability (file: r3/vulnerability-writeup/SKILL.md)\n- cross-review: Cross review code using a subagent with a specified model. Use when the user asks to review code changes AND specifies a model to use (e.g.