{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:04:41.699Z","ordinal":68044,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d1d258d1-f123-4282-9421-a0c56c210304","process_id":"64885","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg '^# (tests|pass|fail)|^not ok' /tmp/testcenter-participant-http-auth-units-final.log | tail -8\nrg '^ui_smoke_step=|Error|AssertionError|TimeoutError|UI smoke stopped' /tmp/testcenter-participant-http-auth-ui-gate.log | tail -8\nrg -n 'ParticipantSignIn|token|session' README.md | tail -12\nsed -n '4490,4505p' apps/api/src/index.ts\nsed -n '2198,2215p' apps/api/src/index.ts"],"cwd":"file:///Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg '^# (tests|pass|fail)|''^not ok' /tmp/testcenter-participant-http-auth-units-final.log","query":"^# (tests|pass|fail)|^not ok","path":"testcenter-participant-http-auth-units-final.log"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg '^ui_smoke_step=|Error|AssertionError|TimeoutError|UI smoke stopped' /tmp/testcenter-participant-http-auth-ui-gate.log","query":"^ui_smoke_step=|Error|AssertionError|TimeoutError|UI smoke stopped","path":"testcenter-participant-http-auth-ui-gate.log"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'ParticipantSignIn|token|session' README.md","query":"ParticipantSignIn|token|session","path":"README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '4490,4505p' apps/api/src/index.ts","name":"index.ts","path":"apps/api/src/index.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '2198,2215p' apps/api/src/index.ts","name":"index.ts","path":"apps/api/src/index.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\n# tests 140\n# pass 140\n# fail 0\n# tests 17\n# pass 17\n# fail 0\nui_smoke_step=action-previous-unit-start\nui_smoke_step=action-previous-unit-done\nui_smoke_step=action-complete-test-start\nui_smoke_step=action-complete-test-done\nui_smoke_step=participant-entry-completed-session-reentry\nui_smoke_step=participant-entry-clear-session\nui_smoke_step=participant-verona-player\nui_smoke_step=participant-verona-offline-outbox\n813:- monitor controls let authorized operators pause, resume, complete, lock or unlock the entire test, globally unlock or re-lock participant navigation, set a timed block's replacement rest time, or force an open run to a selected unit from the operator shell; whole-test locking is persisted independently from pause/running status, blocks participant mutations with an explicit response, remains visible in starter/open-run cards and CSV exports, and honors imported `lock_test_on_termination` by retaining the current unit for a monitor-authorized continuation. The persisted monitor target is separate from the participant's current unit and drives both single-run and batch go-to/time commands, while old browser snapshots hydrate it from the prior shared value. Scoped monitors receive ordered, adaptivity-aware block choices from the open-run read model; after a successful jump, imported `autoselectNextBlock=\"yes\"` profiles prepare the following visible block for the next click and clear the target after the final block, matching the original double-click workflow. Visible runs can be added to an exact-id batch preview and are confirmation-gated before a bounded, deduplicated best-effort dispatch whose response separates successes from per-run failures and leaves failures selected for retry; global navigation unlock durably bypasses code, leave-lock, and completeness guards without changing run status or reopening elapsed timed blocks, navigation re-lock restores authored rules for subsequent actions without reconstructing already consumed one-time gates, replacement time is parked until entry when the block is not current, and supervised go-to targets an exact unit, clears its code/leave locks, and reopens its closed timed block with the configured duration. Open-run cards, direct filters, imported monitor profiles, and CSV exports now expose the original Booklet Species (`species: N`, counting top-level testlets); their card layout applies imported `full`, `medium`, and `small` profile density as one-column, responsive medium, and compact responsive presentations. The Ops view includes a structured monitor-profile editor for layout settings, built-in visibility flags, and nested run filters; it can prepare profiles for a new monitor account or update the durable profile set of an existing scoped role without raw JSON. Every successful command persists a `monitor_run_command_issued` workspace activity event, surfaces filterable history acknowledgements, and keeps the open-run/read-model state in sync. The Runtime view now opens the authenticated workspace monitor event stream, displays its connection and last-event state, refreshes on versioned snapshot/change messages, reconnects automatically, and falls back to polling without treating computed countdown seconds as material changes. Scoped monitor selection stays within monitor-authorized reads and does not request participant-session details\n814:- scoped monitor sessions additionally receive a profile-aware live dashboard over the same authorized open-run read model: visible runs, unique participants, running/paused/locked counts, and group totals update with monitor events. Group cards aggregate participant/run counts, booklet, current block, timer, and latest-activity context and can apply the corresponding open-run group filter without broadening server scope\n830:- the shell persists non-secret form context locally, exposes guided flows for admin bootstrap/sign-in, admin-session reads, admin user management with selectable role-assignment cards and filtered admin-user/audit reads plus admin-user/audit CSV export, tenant/workspace directory selection and CSV export, workspace bootstrap, workspace overview CSV export, file-backed source-document loading with draft preview for XML/JSON/manifest files, import, filtered source-package/import-job/content-release CSV export, runtime with a non-persisted participant-password field, persisted participant roster import/listing/export with validation warnings and local parse preview, a participant launchpad for roster/link/session handoff, participant route session re-entry and local leave/reset, participant-entry API-error guidance for ambiguous workspace and launch issues, CSV/XML/JSON entry-link preview/download, filtered content reads, filtered participant-session/response/review reads and CSV exports, participant test-log inspection plus original-style CSV export, selected-group Original-compatible result archives containing response/log/review CSV and JSON reports, filtered workspace activity reads plus a separate audit CSV export, study-monitor booklet/unit/run progress, monitor status/group/booklet/unit cards that seed participant-matrix filters, a monitor review queue with focused response/review handoff, direct Runtime handoff from monitor run, run-detail review, and unit-detail run cards plus Runtime preparation from monitor detail roster cards, and study-monitor summary/matrix/run-detail CSV export, surfaces operational summaries plus an activity feed, switches authenticated study/group monitors into a reduced role-aware console that performs only monitor-authorized reads, and now has repo-native browser smoke coverage for the runtime lifecycle, blocked activation guard, failed-import retry flow, protected admin directory, tenant/workspace directory export, workspace overview export, file-backed manifest loading, source-package/import-job/content-release CSV export, CSV/XML/JSON participant roster entry-link generation/export, participant launchpad state, typed group-result archive and deletion flows, study-monitor booklet/unit/run progress/export, admin-session reads, admin-user/audit CSV export, response/review/test-log/activity CSV export, operator timeline/session/content/runtime filters, open-run selection filter sync, group-monitor UI isolation, activation-blocking runtime handoff, run-detail review handoff, and unit-detail review handoff\n831:- participant-matrix retrieval now keeps a 200-row server window independent from the operator's visible-card limit, so totals and hidden-row counts remain correct beyond 25 rows; detailed response cards always expose both session and test-run identity, including when a roster display name is present\n903:npm run smoke:ui:admin-session-bulk\n924:The `smoke:ui:content` variant is a fast browser slice that stops after admin/workspace bootstrap, original loose multi-file upload, automatic transitive workspace-dependency capture, explicit fallback assembly, source-package import, release activation, and the content prompt read model; it also verifies direct unit `Definition` prompt extraction. The `smoke:ui:system-check` variant executes both original system-check definitions, gates the anonymous report-save dialog plus success redirect, migrates several original-format JSON reports through Angular, verifies resumable duplicate detection across a multi-check batch, and downloads legacy-compatible CSV plus JSON. The `smoke:ui:system-check-access` variant continues through operational-login migration and proves that creating the first dedicated system-check account atomically replaces the public anonymous Start action with protected account entry, including password rotation, single-check auto-selection, required-field validation, a real report save with the forced login title, success redirect, and route isolation. The `smoke:ui:json-roster` variant continues through CSV/XML/original Testcenter `Login`/JSON roster import, saved roster export, and generated participant entry links. The `smoke:ui:participant-entry` variant continues through participant-route action gating, automatic single-Booklet sign-in, start/resume, session re-entry, direct `Definition` prompt display, completion, and local leave/reset. The `smoke:ui:participant-code` variant stops after verifying the original password-first `<Booklet codes>` challenge, invalid-code guidance, code-scoped session creation, and non-persistence of the code in browser storage. The `smoke:ui:activation-roster-warnings` variant continues to the staged-release roster compatibility warning drill-down before stopping. The `smoke:ui:review-readiness` variant continues through participant start, detailed response filtering, review creation/filtering, and the runtime review-readiness checklist. The `smoke:ui:monitor-review` variant continues through the study-monitor review queue and verifies the focused response/review handoff into Runtime. The `smoke:ui:monitor-detail-review` variant verifies booklet-detail and group-detail response/review handoffs into Runtime. The `smoke:ui:participant-detail-review` variant verifies the participant-matrix drill-down and participant-detail response/review handoff into Runtime. The `smoke:ui:monitor-bulk` variant verifies exact-id selection, confirmation, bulk pause/resume responses, and live run-state reconciliation. The `smoke:ui:delete-group-results` variant verifies result-group selection, the three selected-group CSV downloads, workspace-key-confirmed aggregate deletion, and its post-delete read-model/activity effects. The `smoke:ui:admin-session-bulk` variant verifies exact active-session selection, signed-in-session exclusion, labelled in-app confirmation, server-side delegation/audit enforcement, revocation of two live delegated bearer sessions, and automatic token/session cleanup plus reload in a second browser whose exact session was revoked. The `smoke:ui:admin-password-reset-confirmation` variant verifies the shared confirmation's safe initial focus and Escape cancellation before explicitly approving the reset, then proves old-password invalidation and the mandatory next-login change. The `smoke:ui:admin-password-change` variant covers the global account identity/role/scope panel and operator-shell sign-out plus the mandatory post-reset change and voluntary self-service path, including current-password rejection, double entry, complete session revocation, old-password invalidation, and renewed sign-in. The `smoke:ui:admin-password-bulk` variant generates a distinct 24-character password for each selected account, applies every reset through the existing delegation boundary, verifies old/new sign-in behavior, and validates the one-time CSV handoff plus in-memory cleanup. The `smoke:ui:admin-role-bulk` variant reuses the bounded exact account selection to assign one scoped role to two accounts through independent delegation checks and audit events, retaining only failures for retry. The `smoke:ui:admin-status-bulk` variant disables two delegated accounts through Angular, proves their live bearer tokens are rejected, and confirms that both session IDs are formally visible as revoked. The `smoke:ui:admin-delete` variant drives the shared confirmation across the preceding account mutations, permanently deletes two delegated accounts through Angular, verifies their directory and session removal, and requires retained deletion audits with exact role/session counts. The full SQLite variants build the Angular frontend, boot the built API process on SQLite, and drive a real browser through:\n926:- admin bootstrap, current-session, sign-out, sign-in, mandatory and current-password-verified voluntary self-service password changes, protected tenant/workspace directory reads, protected admin-user and audit read models plus their filters, admin-user creation, individual and bounded unique-password batch resets, scoped role assignment/revocation, bounded best-effort session revocation, status deactivation with cascading live-session revocation, and confirmed permanent account deletion with retained audit evidence\n930:- participant sign-in, optional participant-password entry, original per-booklet second-code challenge, code-scoped session reuse, session resume, direct `Definition` prompt display, and participant completion\n932:- CSV/TSV/semicolon roster import with canonical or alias headers, XML/original Testcenter `Login`/JSON participant roster import including password-required metadata, participant-session export, and open-run export through the runtime shell\n954:The STARS corpus retains the byte-exact metadata-2.0/API-6 Player from a fixed official Testbed commit and a radio-button definition from the matching 0.6.19 source tag as historical independent-family coverage. It also pins the current official 0.7.2 release and its byte-exact BUTTONS option-text definition from the same source tag; production SQLite/Chromium gates `stars-unit-definition@5.3`, persists its `iqb-standard@2.0` choice in JSON-string `responses`, and restores the selection after reload. Separately, the current Original Testcenter package pins the complete 0.6.40 Player/Unit/Voud/Vomd/28-alias Booklet/Testtakers graph. Its production SQLite/Chromium gate imports the unmodified assets, signs in through the original hot-return account, persists `iqb-standard@2.0` responses on aliases `1` and `2`, follows the Player's continue navigation, and restores the second selected option after reload. The dedicated `smoke:ui:stars-recovery` slice additionally proves that the bounded 200-entry browser outbox retains 56 alias-scoped responses from two valid participant runs across one actual hard reload with the active save route unavailable. It restores the visible response semantically after Player JSON reserialization, drains only that run with its visible Unit first, retains the other run exactly until its own session opens and drains visible-Unit-first, then mirrors a separate 28-Unit queue into IndexedDB on page close, replays it idempotently, and leaves both queues empty. A separate mid-drain reload settles seven of 28 responses, retains exactly the remaining 21 across the Player restart, tolerates th