bounded best-effort session revocation, status deactivation with cascading live-session revocation, and confirmed permanent account deletion with retained audit evidence\n930:- participant sign-in, optional participant-password entry, original per-booklet second-code challenge, code-scoped session reuse, session resume, direct `Definition` prompt display, and participant completion\n932:- CSV/TSV/semicolon roster import with canonical or alias headers, XML/original Testcenter `Login`/JSON participant roster import including password-required metadata, participant-session export, and open-run export through the runtime shell\n954:The STARS corpus retains the byte-exact metadata-2.0/API-6 Player from a fixed official Testbed commit and a radio-button definition from the matching 0.6.19 source tag as historical independent-family coverage. It also pins the current official 0.7.2 release and its byte-exact BUTTONS option-text definition from the same source tag; production SQLite/Chromium gates `stars-unit-definition@5.3`, persists its `iqb-standard@2.0` choice in JSON-string `responses`, and restores the selection after reload. Separately, the current Original Testcenter package pins the complete 0.6.40 Player/Unit/Voud/Vomd/28-alias Booklet/Testtakers graph. Its production SQLite/Chromium gate imports the unmodified assets, signs in through the original hot-return account, persists `iqb-standard@2.0` responses on aliases `1` and `2`, follows the Player's continue navigation, and restores the second selected option after reload. The dedicated `smoke:ui:stars-recovery` slice additionally proves that the bounded 200-entry browser outbox retains 56 alias-scoped responses from two valid participant runs across one actual hard reload with the active save route unavailable. It restores the visible response semantically after Player JSON reserialization, drains only that run with its visible Unit first, retains the other run exactly until its own session opens and drains visible-Unit-first, then mirrors a separate 28-Unit queue into IndexedDB on page close, replays it idempotently, and leaves both queues empty. A separate mid-drain reload settles seven of 28 responses, retains exactly the remaining 21 across the Player restart, tolerates the idempotent visible-Unit reserialization, and finishes with all server responses committed and the browser queue empty. A complete Chromium browser-process crash after the origin store has settled, followed by relaunch from the same persistent profile, proves that another complete 28-Unit queue drains without any `pagehide` handoff. At the storage boundary, a full 200-entry outbox rejects a 201st independent Unit instead of silently evicting an older response; the Participant sees the failed save, every secured entry remains byte-for-byte present, and an explicit retry persists the current answer after capacity is released.\n966:The `smoke:ui:operator-auth` variant repeats the browser flow with `FIRST_SLICE_OPERATOR_AUTH_REQUIRED=true`, verifying that the shell can carry the admin bearer session into protected operator routes. The `smoke:ui:postgres` variant migrates the configured Postgres database first, then runs the protected browser flow against the Postgres-backed API.\n1039:- participant launch is still simplified, but now supports one-step starter launch, explicit tenant/workspace scoping with ambiguous workspace-key rejection, group keys, optional roster-password checks, original per-booklet second-code challenges with code-scoped durable sessions, saved-roster display context, ordered multi-booklet assignments—including differently preset variants of the same source booklet—with available/in-progress/completed starter state and sequential runs in one participant session, booklet selection on participant entry links, and booklet-scoped unit validation when saving progress\n    const userAgentHeader = request.headers[\"user-agent\"];\n    const requestUserAgent = Array.isArray(userAgentHeader)\n      ? userAgentHeader[0] ?? null\n      : userAgentHeader ?? null;\n\n    try {\n      await authorizeParticipantRoute(services, request, pathname);\n      if (request.method === \"GET\" && isParticipantEntryPath(pathname)) {\n        sendRedirect(response, 302, `/app/participant${url.search}`);\n        return;\n      }\n\n      if (request.method === \"GET\" && isSystemCheckEntryPath(pathname)) {\n        sendRedirect(response, 302, `/app/system-check${url.search}`);\n        return;\n      }\n\nconst isFirstSliceError = (value: unknown): value is FirstSliceError =>\n  value instanceof Error &&\n  \"statusCode\" in value &&\n  \"errorCode\" in value;\n\nconst createRoutePattern = (template: string): RegExp =>\n  new RegExp(\n    `^${template\n      .replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, \"\\\\$&\")\n      .replace(/:([A-Za-z0-9_]+)/g, \"(?<$1>[^/]+)\")}$`\n  );\n\nconst adminUserUpdatePattern = createRoutePattern(\n  productionApiRoutes.admin.updateUser\n);\nconst adminUserResetPasswordPattern = createRoutePattern(\n  productionApiRoutes.admin.resetPassword\n"},"started_at_ms":1791050681698,"completed_at_ms":1791050681699}}
