{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:32:55.900Z","ordinal":68413,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac14a54379c87d2aad8cbc739675dad","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Die echte Abmeldung ist jetzt im sichtbaren Browser bestanden: Fehler und erneuter Versuch funktionieren, der alte Schlüssel wird ungültig, und nach Wiederanmeldung erscheint dieselbe gespeicherte Antwort im selben Testlauf. Auch der schmale Bildschirm und die Tastaturbedienung sind geprüft. Der größere geschützte Regressionstest läuft noch.\n"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634","create_time":1791052344.621273,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac14a54379c87d2aad8cbc739675dad","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a1030a-675b-7823-be4f-c201c9c96b51","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":86}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:33:34.749Z","ordinal":68414,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac14a57e33487d2a964f8b6942130b9","status":"completed","call_id":"call_DeMxIdZOrS2kHHtUE9IDf9at","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/README.md\\n@@\\n-server and can resume the same run; `Leave Session` remains the separate local\\n-sign-out action.\\n+server and can resume the same run; `Leave Session` remains the separate local\\n+session-clear action, not server credential revocation.\\n@@\\n-close on their next authorization check. The optional Original account logout\\n-control remains disabled until its own UI lifecycle gate is implemented.\\n+close on their next authorization check. On the optional Original Starter,\\n+open `Nutzerinformationen` and choose `Abmelden` to revoke participant access.\\n+The client waits for confirmation before returning to login. A failure leaves\\n+the account menu open for retry; neither saved responses nor pending answer\\n+queues are deleted. A concurrent renewed login or a different active\\n+participant is not cleared by a stale logout completion. Re-entry through real\\n+credentials restores the same resumable run and its responses with a new key.\\n+The Rewrite `Leave Session` action still clears only the local view.\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\\n@@\\n-  action does not establish this guarantee; Original-preview sign-out stays\\n-  disabled until this server boundary has been implemented and verified.\\n+  action does not establish this guarantee. The Original-preview account now\\n+  exposes the separately verified server-backed logout described below.\\n@@\\n-  preserved access expiry and workspace-deletion cleanup. This service is not\\n-  yet exposed as a UI logout operation: the Original account action remains\\n-  disabled until the newly enforced HTTP transport passes its browser gates.\\n+  preserved access expiry and workspace-deletion cleanup. The HTTP boundary\\n+  and Original Starter account logout now use this service; local session\\n+  clearing remains a distinct operation.\\n@@\\n-  store); seventeen frontend/worker/test-actor tests passed. PostgreSQL and\\n-  its current PostgreSQL gate remains pending. A fresh protected SQLite/\\n+  store); seventeen frontend/worker/test-actor tests passed. The PostgreSQL\\n+  integration gate and all three Compose PostgreSQL smoke variants passed in\\n+  the HTTP-ownership checkpoint's CI run. That run is not overall green:\\n+  repeated Test Controller setup logins rotate credentials that the browser\\n+  then incorrectly reuses. These fixtures are being corrected through real UI\\n+  reauthentication without relaxing owner checks. A fresh protected SQLite/\\n@@\\n-  yet the full browser/visual matrix or the enabled Original logout action.\\n+  yet the full browser/visual matrix.\\n@@\\n   tests re-authenticate through the real UI before resuming the first browser.\\n+  Original Starter logout waits for actual HTTP revocation before clearing the\\n+  visible session. Errors stay in the open account menu for retry. The local\\n+  credential tombstone uses compare-and-forget; a renewed key or a different\\n+  active participant is not cleared by a stale completion. Pending foreground\\n+  and worker answer queues remain intact. Twenty-five frontend/worker/test-actor/\\n+  logout-state regressions passed. A headful Chromium/owned-SQLite check passed\\n+  a real Player answer save, temporary logout failure and retry, old-key 401,\\n+  real re-login with the same run and byte-identical saved response restored in\\n+  the Player, desktop focus and mobile keyboard logout without overflow or\\n+  page errors. The production frontend remains 469.00kB under the unchanged\\n+  470kB error budget. Full integrated CI and equal-reference visual comparisons\\n+  remain separate acceptance gates.\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md\\n@@\\n-surface gate. Remaining sidebar contents, account sign-out, dialogs and matching\\n+surface gate. Remaining sidebar contents, dialogs and matching\\n@@\\n-sign-out control is explicitly disabled in\\n-this development preview until the backend can reproduce Original\\n-`deletePersonToken`: revoke access without deleting responses, issue a fresh\\n-credential on re-entry, and keep the old credential invalid. Local\\n-`clearSession` is not equivalent to that operation. This remains a functional\\n-requirement as well as an open account-menu interaction state.\\n+sign-out control now reproduces the verified access lifecycle of Original\\n+`deletePersonToken`: revoke access without deleting responses, issue a fresh\\n+credential on re-entry, and keep the old credential invalid. Local\\n+`clearSession` is not equivalent to that operation. Logout waits for server\\n+confirmation; a failed attempt keeps the account menu and error notice open\\n+for retry. It preserves pending answer queues and does not erase a concurrently\\n+renewed key or another participant's visible session. A headful Chromium/\\n+owned-SQLite check passed an actual Player answer save, temporary failure,\\n+successful retry, old-key rejection, real UI re-login into the same run and\\n+byte-identical answer restoration, desktop focus and mobile keyboard logout.\\n+Twenty-five frontend/worker/test-actor/logout-state tests passed. The current\\n+production bundle is 469.00kB, below the unchanged 470kB error threshold.\\n+The larger integrated gate and matching-reference screenshots are still open;\\n+this closes the logout interaction, not the complete visual-parity row.\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff --check; tail -n 4 /tmp/testcenter-participant-logout-controller-ui-gate.log; rg -n '^ui_smoke_step=' /tmp/testcenter-participant-logout-controller-ui-gate.log | tail -n 10; shasum -a 256 docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx; node --check scripts/smoke-ui.mjs\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",\"max_output_tokens\":1200,\"login\":false}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634","create_time":1791052344.621273}}}
