{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:38:06.899Z","ordinal":68500,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a5aef2f7-790e-48b8-aae5-2bbc17d88962","process_id":"80191","command":["/bin/zsh","-c","sed -n '1,200p' apps/web/src/app/bug-report.service.ts; sed -n '1,118p' docs/PARITY.md; rg -n '^ui_smoke_step=' /tmp/testcenter-participant-logout-full-ui-gate.log | tail -n 5; git status --short; git log -4 --format='%h %s'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,200p' apps/web/src/app/bug-report.service.ts; sed -n '1,118p' docs/PARITY.md; rg -n '^ui_smoke_step=' /tmp/testcenter-participant-logout-full-ui-gate.log | tail -n 5; git status --short; git log -4 --format='%h %s'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"import { Injectable, inject, signal } from \"@angular/core\";\n\nimport {\n  buildBugReportText,\n  productionApiRoutes,\n  type BugReportConfigResponse,\n  type SubmitBugReportResponse\n} from \"@testcenter-rewrite-app/contracts\";\n\nimport { RewriteAppApiService } from \"./rewrite-app-api.service\";\n\ntype BugReportStatus =\n  | { kind: \"idle\"; message: \"\" }\n  | { kind: \"working\" | \"success\" | \"error\"; message: string };\n\n@Injectable({ providedIn: \"root\" })\nexport class BugReportService {\n  readonly isOpen = signal(false);\n  readonly reportText = signal(\"\");\n  readonly config = signal<BugReportConfigResponse>({\n    enabled: false,\n    target: null\n  });\n  readonly status = signal<BugReportStatus>({ kind: \"idle\", message: \"\" });\n  readonly issueUrl = signal<string | null>(null);\n\n  private readonly api = inject(RewriteAppApiService);\n  private readonly previousErrors: string[] = [];\n\n  constructor() {\n    void this.loadConfig();\n  }\n\n  async loadConfig(): Promise<void> {\n    try {\n      const { payload } = await this.api.send<BugReportConfigResponse>(\n        \"GET\",\n        productionApiRoutes.system.getBugReportConfig\n      );\n      this.config.set(payload);\n    } catch {\n      this.config.set({ enabled: false, target: null });\n    }\n  }\n\n  capture(error: unknown, buildRef?: string | null): void {\n    const normalized = this.normalizeError(error);\n    this.openReport({\n      label: normalized.label,\n      message: normalized.message,\n      stack: normalized.stack,\n      buildRef\n    });\n  }\n\n  openForMessage(message: string, buildRef?: string | null): void {\n    this.openReport({\n      label: \"ApplicationError\",\n      message,\n      stack: null,\n      buildRef\n    });\n  }\n\n  close(): void {\n    this.isOpen.set(false);\n  }\n\n  async copy(): Promise<void> {\n    try {\n      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.reportText());\n      this.status.set({ kind: \"success\", message: \"Fehlerbericht kopiert.\" });\n    } catch {\n      this.status.set({\n        kind: \"error\",\n        message: \"Der Fehlerbericht konnte nicht kopiert werden. Bitte herunterladen.\"\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  download(): void {\n    const objectUrl = URL.createObjectURL(\n      new Blob([this.reportText()], { type: \"text/plain;charset=utf-8\" })\n    );\n    const link = document.createElement(\"a\");\n    link.href = objectUrl;\n    link.download = \"bug-report.txt\";\n    link.click();\n    URL.revokeObjectURL(objectUrl);\n    this.status.set({\n      kind: \"success\",\n      message: \"Fehlerbericht heruntergeladen.\"\n    });\n  }\n\n  async submit(): Promise<void> {\n    if (!this.config().enabled || this.status().kind === \"working\") {\n      return;\n    }\n    this.status.set({ kind: \"working\", message: \"Fehlerbericht wird gesendet …\" });\n    this.issueUrl.set(null);\n    try {\n      const { payload } = await this.api.send<SubmitBugReportResponse>(\n        \"POST\",\n        productionApiRoutes.system.submitBugReport,\n        {\n          title: `Testcenter runtime error ${this.readErrorId()}`,\n          tag: \"Runtime Error\",\n          report: this.reportText()\n        }\n      );\n      this.issueUrl.set(payload.issueUrl);\n      this.status.set({ kind: \"success\", message: payload.message });\n    } catch (error) {\n      this.status.set({\n        kind: \"error\",\n        message: this.api.isApiError(error)\n          ? error.message\n          : \"Der Fehlerbericht konnte nicht gesendet werden. Bitte herunterladen.\"\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  private openReport(input: {\n    label: string;\n    message: string;\n    stack: string | null;\n    buildRef?: string | null;\n  }): void {\n    const errorId = globalThis.crypto?.randomUUID?.() ?? `${Date.now()}`;\n    this.reportText.set(\n      buildBugReportText({\n        errorId,\n        label: input.label,\n        message: input.message,\n        timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n        url: globalThis.location?.href ?? \"unknown\",\n        userAgent: globalThis.navigator?.userAgent ?? \"unknown\",\n        buildRef: input.buildRef,\n        stack: input.stack,\n        previousErrors: this.previousErrors\n      })\n    );\n    this.previousErrors.push(`${input.label}: ${input.message}`);\n    if (this.previousErrors.length > 5) {\n      this.previousErrors.shift();\n    }\n    this.issueUrl.set(null);\n    this.status.set({ kind: \"idle\", message: \"\" });\n    this.isOpen.set(true);\n  }\n\n  private readErrorId(): string {\n    return /^Error ID: (.+)$/m.exec(this.reportText())?.[1] ?? \"unknown\";\n  }\n\n  private normalizeError(error: unknown): {\n    label: string;\n    message: string;\n    stack: string | null;\n  } {\n    if (error instanceof Error) {\n      return {\n        label: error.name || \"Error\",\n        message: error.message || String(error),\n        stack: error.stack ?? null\n      };\n    }\n    let message: string;\n    try {\n      message = typeof error === \"string\"\n        ? error\n        : JSON.stringify(error) || String(error);\n    } catch {\n      message = String(error);\n    }\n    return {\n      label: \"UnhandledError\",\n      message,\n      stack: null\n    };\n  }\n}\n# Testcenter parity checklist\n\n## Current 19.0 delta to verify\n\nOn 2026-10-03, the Original fetch advanced to\n`c35cff81383949b4664e0fdffa3ba1154d144d9d` (version 19.0). The broad historical\naudit below remains useful, but its 94% estimate is **not a verified estimate\nagainst 19.0** and does not include the newly requested identical optional UI.\nThe following additional acceptance requirements come from the 19.0 changelog\nand implementation. Each needs current rewrite evidence before it is closed:\n\n- Required current-password confirmation for self-service password changes\n  and for superadmin deletion of administrators/workspaces; resetting another\n  administrator's password retains its distinct authorization boundary.\n- Optional installation-wide refusal of passwordless logins and rejection of\n  Testtakers files containing them, with the Original `sys-check-login` exception.\n  Implemented through `REQUIRE_LOGIN_PASSWORD` (default false): existing\n  passwordless participant sign-in/starter launch and direct/packaged roster\n  imports are refused before roster changes or release staging. Monitor\n  migration candidates also require source passwords; `sys-check-login`\n  candidates remain importable without one. The rewrite's separately created\n  operator accounts still require passwords; passwordless system-check-account\n  sign-in is not claimed as Original UI/auth parity. Regression gates exercise\n  durable policy changes, all six participant modes and both monitor modes,\n  CSV/JSON/XML/ZIP input, unchanged existing passwords/candidates, and startup\n  rejection of invalid settings or conflicting passwordless demo bootstrap.\n- Login codes and `CodeToEnter` are case-insensitive; successful login resets\n  failed-attempt counters. Current execution-mode/session reuse capabilities\n  must agree with the Original definitions.\n  The complete six-mode run-capability/label matrix is now pinned to 19.0 and\n  regression-compared. `run-demo` creates a new session/run on credential entry;\n  explicit session links still address the existing session. Second codes now\n  compare ASCII case-insensitively throughout assignment filtering, starter\n  visibility and session reuse, matching `Login::codeExists`/`SessionDAO` at\n  `c35cff81`. New sessions retain the authored code spelling; older sessions\n  with another spelling remain reusable without rewriting their identity or\n  extending their access window. First login names and passwords remain exact.\n  Successful fresh and reused sign-ins reset only that tenant/workspace/login's\n  failure counter in all four adapters; an active lockout still rejects even\n  the correct password. Memory/file/SQLite API gates cover mixed-case codes,\n  re-imported spelling, assignment isolation, both entry routes, durable\n  restart, independent login counters, and unchanged lockout enforcement.\n  Existing `CodeToEnter` comparison already ignores case; its durable unlock\n  gate covers uppercase and mixed-case input. PostgreSQL remains CI-gated.\n- Default XML XSD validation, supported schema versions and supported\n  `https://w3id.org/iqb/spec/<repo>/<version>` references. Unsupported versions\n  and historical GitHub schema locations are rejected when applying this\n  current contract; the operator file view explains supported versions.\n- Ownership and mode checks for participant answers, unit states, command\n  reads/acknowledgements and Review CRUD; authenticated file paths remain\n  inside their workspace, authenticated downloads use private caching, and\n  internal errors do not disclose server details.\n  Participant account sign-out must also reproduce `deletePersonToken`: revoke\n  its access credential without deleting the session/answers, and re-entry\n  must not reactivate the old credential. The existing local `clearSession`\n  action does not establish this guarantee. The Original-preview account now\n  exposes the separately verified server-backed logout described below.\n  Authenticated downloads now send `Cache-Control: private, no-store`:\n  scoped CSV exports, Original result ZIPs, source packages, Systemcheck and\n  participant Review JSON/CSV (including an empty 204), attachment files/PDFs,\n  and participant resources including HEAD, single/multiple byte ranges and\n  unsatisfied ranges. This reproduces the upstream `FileResponse` shared-cache\n  exclusion and additionally avoids retaining sensitive downloads in the\n  browser cache. Public application assets and hashed frontend files keep\n  their separate cache policies. Current memory/file/SQLite API regressions\n  verify headers alongside exact payload/range behavior; PostgreSQL remains\n  a separate CI gate. This closes the download-cache subrequirement, not\n  participant credential revocation, ownership or internal-error disclosure.\n  The backend credential foundation is implemented separately from session\n  records: random 256-bit tokens, durable SHA-256 digests, permanent revocation\n  tombstones, run-owner binding and compare-and-revoke against a newer login.\n  A legacy opaque session-ID credential is a migration path only until that\n  session's first token issuance or revocation; it cannot reactivate afterward.\n  Unit and memory/file/SQLite store regressions cover rotation, stale logout,\n  cross-participant rejection, restart, unchanged session/run/response records,\n  preserved access expiry and workspace-deletion cleanup. The HTTP boundary\n  and Original Starter account logout now use this service; local session\n  clearing remains a distinct operation.\n  The resource-channel foundation now derives a separate HMAC capability\n  from the durable credential digest and exact session identity. A sandboxed\n  Player can load relative resources without placing the general\n  participant bearer token in its URL. The resource capability cannot authorize\n  answer/Review/command requests, issue another capability or revoke access;\n  credential rotation, revocation and the participant's existing access deadline\n  also invalidate resource access. Unit and memory/file/SQLite regressions prove\n  this separation, cross-session rejection and validity across store restart.\n  HTTP current-state responses now return a resource-only capability path;\n  credential validation precedes resource reads, including HEAD/ranges, and\n  resource path suffixes are redacted from operational logs, including encoded\n  spellings. Public resource preflight remains available without private data.\n  The shared browser request adapter now selects credentials from the exact\n  participant session/run instead of forwarding an operator bearer to public\n  participant routes. Successful participant responses populate a separate,\n  bounded owner/credential store; rotation replaces only the token, and a\n  confirmed-logout tombstone preserves owners and pending answers while\n  disabling local legacy fallback. Participant SSE and worker saves use the\n  same credential selection. Worker credentials are delivery metadata only:\n  answer bytes, request body, delivery ID and foreground outbox stay unchanged.\n  Invalid metadata cannot discard a valid queued answer. Fourteen actual\n  frontend/worker-state tests passed, along with a fresh protected SQLite/\n  Chromium gate through Original/Rewrite entry, real Verona offline recovery\n  and view-closure background delivery; the browser gate rejects operator-token\n  forwarding. A headful check also passed Original footer/account keyboard\n  behavior and same-run return. Successful HTTP sign-in and credential-based\n  launch now issue a fresh participant token. Every known session/run HTTP\n  operation requires its exact owner's credential; neither an operator token,\n  foreign participant token, stable ID nor resource capability can bypass it.\n  DELETE session access returns 205 after compare-and-revoke without deleting\n  the session, run or responses. SSE access is rechecked on each poll and\n  revocation closes an existing stream. A dedicated real HTTP test proves\n  unauthorized reads/writes, preserved execution-mode restrictions, revoked\n  resources/streams, stale-logout rejection and exact response restoration after\n  re-login. The full API suites passed with memory, file and SQLite (161 per\n  store); seventeen frontend/worker/test-actor tests passed. The PostgreSQL\n  integration gate and all three Compose PostgreSQL smoke variants passed in\n  the HTTP-ownership checkpoint's CI run. That run is not overall green:\n  repeated Test Controller setup logins rotate credentials that the browser\n  then incorrectly reuses. These fixtures are being corrected through real UI\n1253:ui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-delete\n1260:ui_smoke_step=nav-content\n1261:ui_smoke_step=assemble-loose-original-source-files\n1271:ui_smoke_step=resolve-loose-original-workspace-dependencies\n1285:ui_smoke_step=resolve-ambiguous-workspace-dependency\n M README.md\n M apps/web/src/app/original-participant-account.component.ts\n M apps/web/src/app/participant-access-credentials.ts\n M apps/web/src/app/participant-view.facade.ts\n M docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md\n M docs/PARITY.md\n M package.json\n M scripts/participant-access-credentials.test.mjs\n M scripts/smoke-ui.mjs\n?? apps/web/src/app/participant-sign-out.ts\n?? docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\n?? scripts/participant-sign-out.test.mjs\nd341434b Enforce participant ownership and revocation across HTTP channels\nd208f383 Bind browser and background requests to participant credentials\n8879f43c Separate player resource capabilities from participant access\n15db665f Diagnose workspace refresh interactions in browser gates\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"import { Injectable, inject, signal } from \"@angular/core\";\n\nimport {\n  buildBugReportText,\n  productionApiRoutes,\n  type BugReportConfigResponse,\n  type SubmitBugReportResponse\n} from \"@testcenter-rewrite-app/contracts\";\n\nimport { RewriteAppApiService } from \"./rewrite-app-api.service\";\n\ntype BugReportStatus =\n  | { kind: \"idle\"; message: \"\" }\n  | { kind: \"working\" | \"success\" | \"error\"; message: string };\n\n@Injectable({ providedIn: \"root\" })\nexport class BugReportService {\n  readonly isOpen = signal(false);\n  readonly reportText = signal(\"\");\n  readonly config = signal<BugReportConfigResponse>({\n    enabled: false,\n    target: null\n  });\n  readonly status = signal<BugReportStatus>({ kind: \"idle\", message: \"\" });\n  readonly issueUrl = signal<string | null>(null);\n\n  private readonly api = inject(RewriteAppApiService);\n  private readonly previousErrors: string[] = [];\n\n  constructor() {\n    void this.loadConfig();\n  }\n\n  async loadConfig(): Promise<void> {\n    try {\n      const { payload } = await this.api.send<BugReportConfigResponse>(\n        \"GET\",\n        productionApiRoutes.system.getBugReportConfig\n      );\n      this.config.set(payload);\n    } catch {\n      this.config.set({ enabled: false, target: null });\n    }\n  }\n\n  capture(error: unknown, buildRef?: string | null): void {\n    const normalized = this.normalizeError(error);\n    this.openReport({\n      label: normalized.label,\n      message: normalized.message,\n      stack: normalized.stack,\n      buildRef\n    });\n  }\n\n  openForMessage(message: string, buildRef?: string | null): void {\n    this.openReport({\n      label: \"ApplicationError\",\n      message,\n      stack: null,\n      buildRef\n    });\n  }\n\n  close(): void {\n    this.isOpen.set(false);\n  }\n\n  async copy(): Promise<void> {\n    try {\n      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.reportText());\n      this.status.set({ kind: \"success\", message: \"Fehlerbericht kopiert.\" });\n    } catch {\n      this.status.set({\n        kind: \"error\",\n        message: \"Der Fehlerbericht konnte nicht kopiert werden. Bitte herunterladen.\"\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  download(): void {\n    const objectUrl = URL.createObjectURL(\n      new Blob([this.reportText()], { type: \"text/plain;charset=utf-8\" })\n    );\n    const link = document.createElement(\"a\");\n    link.href = objectUrl;\n    link.download = \"bug-report.txt\";\n    link.click();\n    URL.revokeObjectURL(objectUrl);\n    this.status.set({\n      kind: \"success\",\n      message: \"Fehlerbericht heruntergeladen.\"\n    });\n  }\n\n  async submit(): Promise<void> {\n    if (!this.config().enabled || this.status().kind === \"working\") {\n      return;\n    }\n    this.status.set({ kind: \"working\", message: \"Fehlerbericht wird gesendet …\" });\n    this.issueUrl.set(null);\n    try {\n      const { payload } = await this.api.send<SubmitBugReportResponse>(\n        \"POST\",\n        productionApiRoutes.system.submitBugReport,\n        {\n          title: `Testcenter runtime error ${this.readErrorId()}`,\n          tag: \"Runtime Error\",\n          report: this.reportText()\n        }\n      );\n      this.issueUrl.set(payload.issueUrl);\n      this.status.set({ kind: \"success\", message: payload.message });\n    } catch (error) {\n      this.status.set({\n        kind: \"error\",\n        message: this.api.isApiError(error)\n          ? error.message\n          : \"Der Fehlerbericht konnte nicht gesendet werden. Bitte herunterladen.\"\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  private openReport(input: {\n    label: string;\n    message: string;\n    stack: string | null;\n    buildRef?: string | null;\n  }): void {\n    const errorId = globalThis.crypto?.randomUUID?.() ?? `${Date.now()}`;\n    this.reportText.set(\n      buildBugReportText({\n        errorId,\n        label: input.label,\n        message: input.message,\n        timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n        url: globalThis.location?.href ?? \"unknown\",\n        userAgent: globalThis.navigator?.userAgent ?? \"unknown\",\n        buildRef: input.buildRef,\n        stack: input.stack,\n        previousErrors: this.previousErrors\n      })\n    );\n    this.previousErrors.push(`${input.label}: ${input.message}`);\n    if (this.previousErrors.length > 5) {\n      this.previousErrors.shift();\n    }\n    this.issueUrl.set(null);\n    this.status.set({ kind: \"idle\", message: \"\" });\n    this.isOpen.set(true);\n  }\n\n  private readErrorId(): string {\n    return /^Error ID: (.+)$/m.exec(this.reportText())?.[1] ?? \"unknown\";\n  }\n\n  private normalizeError(error: unknown): {\n    label: string;\n    message: string;\n    stack: string | null;\n  } {\n    if (error instanceof Error) {\n      return {\n        label: error.name || \"Error\",\n        message: error.message || String(error),\n        stack: error.stack ?? null\n      };\n    }\n    let message: string;\n    try {\n      message = typeof error === \"string\"\n        ? error\n        : JSON.stringify(error) || String(error);\n    } catch {\n      message = String(error);\n    }\n    return {\n      label: \"UnhandledError\",\n      message,\n      stack: null\n    };\n  }\n}\n# Testcenter parity checklist\n\n## Current 19.0 delta to verify\n\nOn 2026-10-03, the Original fetch advanced to\n`c35cff81383949b4664e0fdffa3ba1154d144d9d` (version 19.0). The broad historical\naudit below remains useful, but its 94% estimate is **not a verified estimate\nagainst 19.0** and does not include the newly requested identical optional UI.\nThe following additional acceptance requirements come from the 19.0 changelog\nand implementation. Each needs current rewrite evidence before it is closed:\n\n- Required current-password confirmation for self-service password changes\n  and for superadmin deletion of administrators/workspaces; resetting another\n  administrator's password retains its distinct authorization boundary.\n- Optional installation-wide refusal of passwordless logins and rejection of\n  Testtakers files containing them, with the Original `sys-check-login` exception.\n  Implemented through `REQUIRE_LOGIN_PASSWORD` (default false): existing\n  passwordless participant sign-in/starter launch and direct/packaged roster\n  imports are refused before roster changes or release staging. Monitor\n  migration candidates also require source passwords; `sys-check-login`\n  candidates remain importable without one. The rewrite's separately created\n  operator accounts still require passwords; passwordless system-check-account\n  sign-in is not claimed as Original UI/auth parity. Regression gates exercise\n  durable policy changes, all six participant modes and both monitor modes,\n  CSV/JSON/XML/ZIP input, unchanged existing passwords/candidates, and startup\n  rejection of invalid settings or conflicting passwordless demo bootstrap.\n- Login codes and `CodeToEnter` are case-insensitive; successful login resets\n  failed-attempt counters. Current execution-mode/session reuse capabilities\n  must agree with the Original definitions.\n  The complete six-mode run-capability/label matrix is now pinned to 19.0 and\n  regression-compared. `run-demo` creates a new session/run on credential entry;\n  explicit session links still address the existing session. Second codes now\n  compare ASCII case-insensitively throughout assignment filtering, starter\n  visibility and session reuse, matching `Login::codeExists`/`SessionDAO` at\n  `c35cff81`. New sessions retain the authored code spelling; older sessions\n  with another spelling remain reusable without rewriting their identity or\n  extending their access window. First login names and passwords remain exact.\n  Successful fresh and reused sign-ins reset only that tenant/workspace/login's\n  failure counter in all four adapters; an active lockout still rejects even\n  the correct password. Memory/file/SQLite API gates cover mixed-case codes,\n  re-imported spelling, assignment isolation, both entry routes, durable\n  restart, independent login counters, and unchanged lockout enforcement.\n  Existing `CodeToEnter` comparison already ignores case; its durable unlock\n  gate covers uppercase and mixed-case input. PostgreSQL remains CI-gated.\n- Default XML XSD validation, supported schema versions and supported\n  `https://w3id.org/iqb/spec/<repo>/<version>` references. Unsupported versions\n  and historical GitHub schema locations are rejected when applying this\n  current contract; the operator file view explains supported versions.\n- Ownership and mode checks for participant answers, unit states, command\n  reads/acknowledgements and Review CRUD; authenticated file paths remain\n  inside their workspace, authenticated downloads use private caching, and\n  internal errors do not disclose server details.\n  Participant account sign-out must also reproduce `deletePersonToken`: revoke\n  its access credential without deleting the session/answers, and re-entry\n  must not reactivate the old credential. The existing local `clearSession`\n  action does not establish this guarantee. The Original-preview account now\n  exposes the separately verified server-backed logout described below.\n  Authenticated downloads now send `Cache-Control: private, no-store`:\n  scoped CSV exports, Original result ZIPs, source packages, Systemcheck and\n  participant Review JSON/CSV (including an empty 204), attachment files/PDFs,\n  and participant resources including HEAD, single/multiple byte ranges and\n  unsatisfied ranges. This reproduces the upstream `FileResponse` shared-cache\n  exclusion and additionally avoids retaining sensitive downloads in the\n  browser cache. Public application assets and hashed frontend files keep\n  their separate cache policies. Current memory/file/SQLite API regressions\n  verify headers alongside exact payload/range behavior; PostgreSQL remains\n  a separate CI gate. This closes the download-cache subrequirement, not\n  participant credential revocation, ownership or internal-error disclosure.\n  The backend credential foundation is implemented separately from session\n  records: random 256-bit tokens, durable SHA-256 digests, permanent revocation\n  tombstones, run-owner binding and compare-and-revoke against a newer login.\n  A legacy opaque session-ID credential is a migration path only until that\n  session's first token issuance or revocation; it cannot reactivate afterward.\n  Unit and memory/file/SQLite store regressions cover rotation, stale logout,\n  cross-participant rejection, restart, unchanged session/run/response records,\n  preserved access expiry and workspace-deletion cleanup. The HTTP boundary\n  and Original Starter account logout now use this service; local session\n  clearing remains a distinct operation.\n  The resource-channel foundation now derives a separate HMAC capability\n  from the durable credential digest and exact session identity. A sandboxed\n  Player can load relative resources without placing the general\n  participant bearer token in its URL. The resource capability cannot authorize\n  answer/Review/command requests, issue another capability or revoke access;\n  credential rotation, revocation and the participant's existing access deadline\n  also invalidate resource access. Unit and memory/file/SQLite regressions prove\n  this separation, cross-session rejection and validity across store restart.\n  HTTP current-state responses now return a resource-only capability path;\n  credential validation precedes resource reads, including HEAD/ranges, and\n  resource path suffixes are redacted from operational logs, including encoded\n  spellings. Public resource preflight remains available without private data.\n  The shared browser request adapter now selects credentials from the exact\n  participant session/run instead of forwarding an operator bearer to public\n  participant routes. Successful participant responses populate a separate,\n  bounded owner/credential store; rotation replaces only the token, and a\n  confirmed-logout tombstone preserves owners and pending answers while\n  disabling local legacy fallback. Participant SSE and worker saves use the\n  same credential selection. Worker credentials are delivery metadata only:\n  answer bytes, request body, delivery ID and foreground outbox stay unchanged.\n  Invalid metadata cannot discard a valid queued answer. Fourteen actual\n  frontend/worker-state tests passed, along with a fresh protected SQLite/\n  Chromium gate through Original/Rewrite entry, real Verona offline recovery\n  and view-closure background delivery; the browser gate rejects operator-token\n  forwarding. A headful check also passed Original footer/account keyboard\n  behavior and same-run return. Successful HTTP sign-in and credential-based\n  launch now issue a fresh participant token. Every known session/run HTTP\n  operation requires its exact owner's credential; neither an operator token,\n  foreign participant token, stable ID nor resource capability can bypass it.\n  DELETE session access returns 205 after compare-and-revoke without deleting\n  the session, run or responses. SSE access is rechecked on each poll and\n  revocation closes an existing stream. A dedicated real HTTP test proves\n  unauthorized reads/writes, preserved execution-mode restrictions, revoked\n  resources/streams, stale-logout rejection and exact response restoration after\n  re-login. The full API suites passed with memory, file and SQLite (161 per\n  store); seventeen frontend/worker/test-actor tests passed. The PostgreSQL\n  integration gate and all three Compose PostgreSQL smoke variants passed in\n  the HTTP-ownership checkpoint's CI run. That run is not overall green:\n  repeated Test Controller setup logins rotate credentials that the browser\n  then incorrectly reuses. These fixtures are being corrected through real UI\n1253:ui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-delete\n1260:ui_smoke_step=nav-content\n1261:ui_smoke_step=assemble-loose-original-source-files\n1271:ui_smoke_step=resolve-loose-original-workspace-dependencies\n1285:ui_smoke_step=resolve-ambiguous-workspace-dependency\n M README.md\n M apps/web/src/app/original-participant-account.component.ts\n M apps/web/src/app/participant-access-credentials.ts\n M apps/web/src/app/participant-view.facade.ts\n M docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md\n M docs/PARITY.md\n M package.json\n M scripts/participant-access-credentials.test.mjs\n M scripts/smoke-ui.mjs\n?? apps/web/src/app/participant-sign-out.ts\n?? docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\n?? scripts/participant-sign-out.test.mjs\nd341434b Enforce participant ownership and revocation across HTTP channels\nd208f383 Bind browser and background requests to participant credentials\n8879f43c Separate player resource capabilities from participant access\n15db665f Diagnose workspace refresh interactions in browser gates\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":9042},"formatted_output":"import { Injectable, inject, signal } from \"@angular/core\";\n\nimport {\n  buildBugReportText,\n  productionApiRoutes,\n  type BugReportConfigResponse,\n  type SubmitBugReportResponse\n} from \"@testcenter-rewrite-app/contracts\";\n\nimport { RewriteAppApiService } from \"./rewrite-app-api.service\";\n\ntype BugReportStatus =\n  | { kind: \"idle\"; message: \"\" }\n  | { kind: \"working\" | \"success\" | \"error\"; message: string };\n\n@Injectable({ providedIn: \"root\" })\nexport class BugReportService {\n  readonly isOpen = signal(false);\n  readonly reportText = signal(\"\");\n  readonly config = signal<BugReportConfigResponse>({\n    enabled: false,\n    target: null\n  });\n  readonly status = signal<BugReportStatus>({ kind: \"idle\", message: \"\" });\n  readonly issueUrl = signal<string | null>(null);\n\n  private readonly api = inject(RewriteAppApiService);\n  private readonly previousErrors: string[] = [];\n\n  constructor() {\n    void this.loadConfig();\n  }\n\n  async loadConfig(): Promise<void> {\n    try {\n      const { payload } = await this.api.send<BugReportConfigResponse>(\n        \"GET\",\n        productionApiRoutes.system.getBugReportConfig\n      );\n      this.config.set(payload);\n    } catch {\n      this.config.set({ enabled: false, target: null });\n    }\n  }\n\n  capture(error: unknown, buildRef?: string | null): void {\n    const normalized = this.normalizeError(error);\n    this.openReport({\n      label: normalized.label,\n      message: normalized.message,\n      stack: normalized.stack,\n      buildRef\n    });\n  }\n\n  openForMessage(message: string, buildRef?: string | null): void {\n    this.openReport({\n      label: \"ApplicationError\",\n      message,\n      stack: null,\n      buildRef\n    });\n  }\n\n  close(): void {\n    this.isOpen.set(false);\n  }\n\n  async copy(): Promise<void> {\n    try {\n      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.reportText());\n      this.status.set({ kind: \"success\", message: \"Fehlerbericht kopiert.\" });\n    } catch {\n      this.status.set({\n        kind: \"error\",\n        message: \"Der Fehlerbericht konnte nicht kopiert werden. Bitte herunterladen.\"\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  download(): void {\n    const objectUrl = URL.createObjectURL(\n      new Blob([this.reportText()], { type: \"text/plain;charset=utf-8\" })\n    );\n    const link = document.createElement(\"a\");\n    link.href = objectUrl;\n    link.download = \"bug-report.txt\";\n    link.click();\n    URL.revokeObjectURL(objectUrl);\n    this.status.set({\n      kind: \"success\",\n      message: \"Fehlerbericht heruntergeladen.\"\n    });\n  }\n\n  async submit(): Promise<void> {\n    if (!this.config().enabled || this.status().kind === \"working\") {\n      return;\n    }\n    this.status.set({ kind: \"working\", message: \"Fehlerbericht wird gesendet …\" });\n    this.issueUrl.set(null);\n    try {\n      const { payload } = await this.api.send<SubmitBugReportResponse>(\n        \"POST\",\n        productionApiRoutes.system.submitBugReport,\n        {\n          title: `Testcenter runtime error ${this.readErrorId()}`,\n          tag: \"Runtime Error\",\n          report: this.reportText()\n        }\n      );\n      this.issueUrl.set(payload.issueUrl);\n      this.status.set({ kind: \"success\", message: payload.message });\n    } catch (error) {\n      this.status.set({\n        kind: \"error\",\n        message: this.api.isApiError(error)\n          ? error.message\n          : \"Der Fehlerbericht konnte nicht gesendet werden. Bitte herunterladen.\"\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  private openReport(input: {\n    label: string;\n    message: string;\n    stack: string | null;\n    buildRef?: string | null;\n  }): void {\n    const errorId = globalThis.crypto?.randomUUID?.() ?? `${Date.now()}`;\n    this.reportText.set(\n      buildBugReportText({\n        errorId,\n        label: input.label,\n        message: input.message,\n        timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n        url: globalThis.location?.href ?? \"unknown\",\n        userAgent: globalThis.navigator?.userAgent ?? \"unknown\",\n        buildRef: input.buildRef,\n        stack: input.stack,\n        previousErrors: this.previousErrors\n      })\n    );\n    this.previousErrors.push(`${input.label}: ${input.message}`);\n    if (this.previousErrors.length > 5) {\n      this.previousErrors.shift();\n    }\n    this.issueUrl.set(null);\n    this.status.set({ kind: \"idle\", message: \"\" });\n    this.isOpen.set(true);\n  }\n\n  private readErrorId(): string {\n    return /^Error ID: (.+)$/m.exec(this.reportText())?.[1] ?? \"unknown\";\n  }\n\n  private normalizeError(error: unknown): {\n    label: string;\n    message: string;\n    stack: string | null;\n  } {\n    if (error instanceof Error) {\n      return {\n        label: error.name || \"Error\",\n        message: error.message || String(error),\n        stack: error.stack ?? null\n      };\n    }\n    let message: string;\n    try {\n      message = typeof error === \"string\"\n        ? error\n        : JSON.stringify(error) || String(error);\n    } catch {\n      message = String(error);\n    }\n    return {\n      label: \"UnhandledError\",\n      message,\n      stack: null\n    };\n  }\n}\n# Testcenter parity checklist\n\n## Current 19.0 delta to verify\n\nOn 2026-10-03, the Original fetch advanced to\n`c35cff81383949b4664e0fdffa3ba1154d144d9d` (version 19.0). The broad historical\naudit below remains useful, but its 94% estimate is **not a verified estimate\nagainst 19.0** and does not include the newly requested identical optional UI.\nThe following additional acceptance requirements come from the 19.0 changelog\nand implementation. Each needs current rewrite evidence before it is closed:\n\n- Required current-password confirmation for self-service password changes\n  and for superadmin deletion of administrators/workspaces; resetting another\n  administrator's password retains its distinct authorization boundary.\n- Optional installation-wide refusal of passwordless logins and rejection of\n  Testtakers files containing them, with the Original `sys-check-login` exception.\n  Implemented through `REQUIRE_LOGIN_PASSWORD` (default false): existing\n  passwordless participant sign-in/starter launch and direct/packaged roster\n  imports are refused before roster changes or release staging. Monitor\n  migration candidates also require source passwords; `sys-check-login`\n  candidates remain importable without one. The rewrite's separately created\n  operator accounts still require passwords; passwordless system-check-account\n  sign-in is not claimed as Original UI/auth parity. Regression gates exercise\n  durable policy changes, all six participant modes and both monitor modes,\n  CSV/JSON/XML/ZIP input, unchanged existing passwords/candidates, and startup\n  rejection of invalid settings or conflicting passwordless demo bootstrap.\n- Login codes and `CodeToEnter` are case-insensitive; successful login resets\n  failed-attempt counters. Current execution-mode/session reuse capabilities\n  must agree with the Original definitions.\n  The complete six-mode run-capability/label matrix is now pinned to 19.0 and\n  regression-compared. `run-demo` creates a new session/run on credential entry;\n  explicit session links still address the existing session. Second codes now\n  compare ASCII case-insensitively throughout assignment filtering, starter\n  visibility and session reuse, matching `Login::codeExists`/`SessionDAO` at\n  `c35cff81`. New sessions retain the authored code spelling; older sessions\n  with another spelling remain reusable without rewriting their identity or\n  extending their access window. First login names and passwords remain exact.\n  Successful fresh and reused sign-ins reset only that tenant/workspace/login's\n  failure counter in all four adapters; an active lockout still rejects even\n  the correct password. Memory/file/SQLite API gates cover mixed-case codes,\n  re-imported spelling, assignment isolation, both entry routes, durable\n  restart, independent login counters, and unchanged lockout enforcement.\n  Existing `CodeToEnter` comparison already ignores case; its durable unlock\n  gate covers uppercase and mixed-case input. PostgreSQL remains CI-gated.\n- Default XML XSD validation, supported schema versions and supported\n  `https://w3id.org/iqb/spec/<repo>/<version>` references. Unsupported versions\n  and historical GitHub schema locations are rejected when applying this\n  current contract; the operator file view explains supported versions.\n- Ownership and mode checks for participant answers, unit states, command\n  reads/acknowledgements and Review CRUD; authenticated file paths remain\n  inside their workspace, authenticated downloads use private caching, and\n  internal errors do not disclose server details.\n  Participant account sign-out must also reproduce `deletePersonToken`: revoke\n  its access credential without deleting the session/answers, and re-entry\n  must not reactivate the old credential. The existing local `clearSession`\n  action does not establish this guarantee. The Original-preview account now\n  exposes the separately verified server-backed logout described below.\n  Authenticated downloads now send `Cache-Control: private, no-store`:\n  scoped CSV exports, Original result ZIPs, source packages, Systemcheck and\n  participant Review JSON/CSV (including an empty 204), attachment files/PDFs,\n  and participant resources including HEAD, single/multiple byte ranges and\n  unsatisfied ranges. This reproduces the upstream `FileResponse` shared-cache\n  exclusion and additionally avoids retaining sensitive downloads in the\n  browser cache. Public application assets and hashed frontend files keep\n  their separate cache policies. Current memory/file/SQLite API regressions\n  verify headers alongside exact payload/range behavior; PostgreSQL remains\n  a separate CI gate. This closes the download-cache subrequirement, not\n  participant credential revocation, ownership or internal-error disclosure.\n  The backend credential foundation is implemented separately from session\n  records: random 256-bit tokens, durable SHA-256 digests, permanent revocation\n  tombstones, run-owner binding and compare-and-revoke against a newer login.\n  A legacy opaque session-ID credential is a migration path only until that\n  session's first token issuance or revocation; it cannot reactivate afterward.\n  Unit and memory/file/SQLite store regressions cover rotation, stale logout,\n  cross-participant rejection, restart, unchanged session/run/response records,\n  preserved access expiry and workspace-deletion cleanup. The HTTP boundary\n  and Original Starter account logout now use this service; local session\n  clearing remains a distinct operation.\n  The resource-channel foundation now derives a separate HMAC capability\n  from the durable credential digest and exact session identity. A sandboxed\n  Player can load relative resources without placing the general\n  participant bearer token in its URL. The resource capability cannot authorize\n  answer/Review/command requests, issue another capability or revoke access;\n  credential rotation, revocation and the participant's existing access deadline\n  also invalidate resource access. Unit and memory/file/SQLite regressions prove\n  this separation, cross-session rejection and validity across store restart.\n  HTTP current-state responses now return a resource-only capability path;\n  credential validation precedes resource reads, including HEAD/ranges, and\n  resource path suffixes are redacted from operational logs, including encoded\n  spellings. Public resource preflight remains available without private data.\n  The shared browser request adapter now selects credentials from the exact\n  participant session/run instead of forwarding an operator bearer to public\n  participant routes. Successful participant responses populate a separate,\n  bounded owner/credential store; rotation replaces only the token, and a\n  confirmed-logout tombstone preserves owners and pending answers while\n  disabling local legacy fallback. Participant SSE and worker saves use the\n  same credential selection. Worker credentials are delivery metadata only:\n  answer bytes, request body, delivery ID and foreground outbox stay unchanged.\n  Invalid metadata cannot discard a valid queued answer. Fourteen actual\n  frontend/worker-state tests passed, along with a fresh protected SQLite/\n  Chromium gate through Original/Rewrite entry, real Verona offline recovery\n  and view-closure background delivery; the browser gate rejects operator-token\n  forwarding. A headful check also passed Original footer/account keyboard\n  behavior and same-run return. Successful HTTP sign-in and credential-based\n  launch now issue a fresh participant token. Every known session/run HTTP\n  operation requires its exact owner's credential; neither an operator token,\n  foreign participant token, stable ID nor resource capability can bypass it.\n  DELETE session access returns 205 after compare-and-revoke without deleting\n  the session, run or responses. SSE access is rechecked on each poll and\n  revocation closes an existing stream. A dedicated real HTTP test proves\n  unauthorized reads/writes, preserved execution-mode restrictions, revoked\n  resources/streams, stale-logout rejection and exact response restoration after\n  re-login. The full API suites passed with memory, file and SQLite (161 per\n  store); seventeen frontend/worker/test-actor tests passed. The PostgreSQL\n  integration gate and all three Compose PostgreSQL smoke variants passed in\n  the HTTP-ownership checkpoint's CI run. That run is not overall green:\n  repeated Test Controller setup logins rotate credentials that the browser\n  then incorrectly reuses. These fixtures are being corrected through real UI\n1253:ui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-delete\n1260:ui_smoke_step=nav-content\n1261:ui_smoke_step=assemble-loose-original-source-files\n1271:ui_smoke_step=resolve-loose-original-workspace-dependencies\n1285:ui_smoke_step=resolve-ambiguous-workspace-dependency\n M README.md\n M apps/web/src/app/original-participant-account.component.ts\n M apps/web/src/app/participant-access-credentials.ts\n M apps/web/src/app/participant-view.facade.ts\n M docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md\n M docs/PARITY.md\n M package.json\n M scripts/participant-access-credentials.test.mjs\n M scripts/smoke-ui.mjs\n?? apps/web/src/app/participant-sign-out.ts\n?? docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\n?? scripts/participant-sign-out.test.mjs\nd341434b Enforce participant ownership and revocation across HTTP channels\nd208f383 Bind browser and background requests to participant credentials\n8879f43c Separate player resource capabilities from participant access\n15db665f Diagnose workspace refresh interactions in browser gates\n"},"started_at_ms":1791052686899,"completed_at_ms":1791052686899}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:38:06.907Z","ordinal":68501,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1030f-263b-7461-9c18-fc5c1794f7c1","call_id":"call_TiTR87h7rFvtmvH9IZs9Ql7f","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"fbd627\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000009042,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3641,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3641)\\nTotal output lines: 322\\n\\nimport { Injectable, inject, signal } from \\\"@angular/core\\\";\\n\\nimport {\\n  buildBugReportText,\\n  productionApiRoutes,\\n  type BugReportConfigResponse,\\n  type SubmitBugReportResponse\\n} from \\\"@testcenter-rewrite-app/contracts\\\";\\n\\nimport { RewriteAppApiService } from \\\"./rewrite-app-api.service\\\";\\n\\ntype BugReportStatus =\\n  | { kind: \\\"idle\\\"; message: \\\"\\\" }\\n  | { kind: \\\"working\\\" | \\\"success\\\" | \\\"error\\\"; message: string };\\n\\n@Injectable({ providedIn: \\\"root\\\" })\\nexport class BugReportService {\\n  readonly isOpen = signal(false);\\n  readonly reportText = signal(\\\"\\\");\\n  readonly config = signal<BugReportConfigResponse>({\\n    enabled: false,\\n    target: null\\n  });\\n  readonly status = signal<BugReportStatus>({ kind: \\\"idle\\\", message: \\\"\\\" });\\n  readonly issueUrl = signal<string | null>(null);\\n\\n  private readonly api = inject(RewriteAppApiService);\\n  private readonly previousErrors: string[] = [];\\n\\n  constructor() {\\n    void this.loadConfig();\\n  }\\n\\n  async loadConfig(): Promise<void> {\\n    try {\\n      const { payload } = await this.api.send<BugReportConfigResponse>(\\n        \\\"GET\\\",\\n        productionApiRoutes.system.getBugReportConfig\\n      );\\n      this.config.set(payload);\\n    } catch {\\n      this.config.set({ enabled: false, target: null });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  capture(error: unknown, buildRef?: string | null): void {\\n    const normalized = this.normalizeError(error);\\n    this.openReport({\\n      label: normalized.label,\\n      message: normalized.message,\\n      stack: normalized.stack,\\n      buildRef\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  openForMessage(message: string, buildRef?: string | null): void {\\n    this.openReport({\\n      label: \\\"ApplicationError\\\",\\n      message,\\n      stack: null,\\n      buildRef\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  close(): void {\\n    this.isOpen.set(false);\\n  }\\n\\n  async copy(): Promise<void> {\\n    try {\\n      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.reportText());\\n      this.status.set({ kind: \\\"success\\\", message: \\\"Fehlerbericht kopiert.\\\" });\\n    } catch {\\n      this.status.set({\\n        kind: \\\"error\\\",\\n        message: \\\"Der Fehlerbericht konnte nicht kopiert werden. Bitte herunterladen.\\\"\\n      });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  download(): void {\\n    const objectUrl = URL.createObjectURL(\\n      new Blob([this.reportText()], { type: \\\"text/plain;charset=utf-8\\\" })\\n    );\\n    const link = document.createElement(\\\"a\\\");\\n    link.href = objectUrl;\\n    link.download = \\\"bug-report.txt\\\";\\n    link.click();\\n    URL.revokeObjectURL(objectUrl);\\n    this.status.set({\\n      kind: \\\"success\\\",\\n      message: \\\"Fehlerbericht heruntergeladen.\\\"\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  async submit(): Promise<void> {\\n    if (!this.config().enabled || this.status().kind === \\\"working\\\") {\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    this.status.set({ kind: \\\"working\\\", message: \\\"Fehlerbericht wird gesendet …\\\" });\\n    this.issueUrl.set(null);\\n    try {\\n      const { payload } = await this.api.send<SubmitBugReportResponse>(\\n        \\\"POST\\\",\\n        productionApiRoutes.system.submitBugReport,\\n        {\\n          title: `Testcenter runtime error ${this.readErrorId()}`,\\n          tag: \\\"Runtime Error\\\",\\n          report: this.reportText()\\n        }\\n      );\\n      this.issueUrl.set(payload.issueUrl);\\n      this.status.set({ kind: \\\"success\\\", message: payload.message });\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      this.status.set({\\n        kind: \\\"error\\\",\\n        message: this.api.isApiError(error)\\n          ? error.message\\n          : \\\"Der Fehlerbericht konnte nicht gesendet werden. Bitte herunterladen.\\\"\\n      });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  private openReport(input: {\\n    label: string;\\n    message: string;\\n    stack: string | null;\\n    buildRef?: string | null;\\n  }): void {\\n    const errorId = globalThis.crypto?.randomUUID?.() ?? `${Date.now()}`;\\n    this.reportText.set(\\n      buildBugReportText({\\n        errorId,\\n        label: input.label,\\n        message: input.message,\\n        timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\\n        url: globalThis.location?.href ?? \\\"unknown\\\",\\n        userAgent: globalThis.navigator?.userAgent ?? \\\"unknown\\\",\\n        buildRef: input.buildRef,\\n        stack: input.stack,\\n        previousErrors: this.previousErrors\\n      })\\n    );\\n    this.previousErrors.push(`${input.label}: ${input.message}`);\\n    if (this.previousErrors.length > 5) {\\n      this.previousErrors.shift();\\n    }\\n    this.issueUrl.set(null);\\n    this.status.set({ kind: \\\"idle\\\", message: \\\"\\\" });\\n    this.isOpen.set(true);\\n  }\\n\\n  private readErrorId(): string {\\n    return /^Error ID: (.+)$/m.exec(this.reportText())?.[1] ?? \\\"unknown\\\";\\n  }\\n\\n  private normalizeError(error: unknown): {\\n    label: string;\\n    message: string;\\n    stack: string | null;\\n  } {\\n    if (error instanceof Error) {\\n      return {\\n        label: error.name || \\\"Error\\\",\\n        message: error.message || String(error),\\n        stack: error.stack ?? null\\n      };\\n    }\\n    let message: string;\\n    try {\\n      message = typeof error === \\\"string\\\"\\n        ? error\\n        : JSON.stringify(error) || String(error);\\n    } catch {\\n      message = String(error);\\n    }\\n    return {\\n      label: \\\"UnhandledError\\\",\\n      message,\\n      stack: null\\n    };\\n  }\\n}\\n# Testcenter parity checklist\\n\\n## Current 19.0 delta to verify\\n\\nOn 2026-10-03, the Original fetch advanced to\\n`c35cff81383949b4664e0fdffa3ba1154d144d9d` (version 19.0). The broad historical\\naudit below remains useful, but its 94% estimate is **not a verified estimate\\nagainst 19.0** and does not include the newly requested identical optional UI.\\nThe following additional acceptance requirements …941 tokens truncated…ent files/PDFs,\\n  and participant resources including HEAD, single/multiple byte ranges and\\n  unsatisfied ranges. This reproduces the upstream `FileResponse` shared-cache\\n  exclusion and additionally avoids retaining sensitive downloads in the\\n  browser cache. Public application assets and hashed frontend files keep\\n  their separate cache policies. Current memory/file/SQLite API regressions\\n  verify headers alongside exact payload/range behavior; PostgreSQL remains\\n  a separate CI gate. This closes the download-cache subrequirement, not\\n  participant credential revocation, ownership or internal-error disclosure.\\n  The backend credential foundation is implemented separately from session\\n  records: random 256-bit tokens, durable SHA-256 digests, permanent revocation\\n  tombstones, run-owner binding and compare-and-revoke against a newer login.\\n  A legacy opaque session-ID credential is a migration path only until that\\n  session's first token issuance or revocation; it cannot reactivate afterward.\\n  Unit and memory/file/SQLite store regressions cover rotation, stale logout,\\n  cross-participant rejection, restart, unchanged session/run/response records,\\n  preserved access expiry and workspace-deletion cleanup. The HTTP boundary\\n  and Original Starter account logout now use this service; local session\\n  clearing remains a distinct operation.\\n  The resource-channel foundation now derives a separate HMAC capability\\n  from the durable credential digest and exact session identity. A sandboxed\\n  Player can load relative resources without placing the general\\n  participant bearer token in its URL. The resource capability cannot authorize\\n  answer/Review/command requests, issue another capability or revoke access;\\n  credential rotation, revocation and the participant's existing access deadline\\n  also invalidate resource access. Unit and memory/file/SQLite regressions prove\\n  this separation, cross-session rejection and validity across store restart.\\n  HTTP current-state responses now return a resource-only capability path;\\n  credential validation precedes resource reads, including HEAD/ranges, and\\n  resource path suffixes are redacted from operational logs, including encoded\\n  spellings. Public resource preflight remains available without private data.\\n  The shared browser request adapter now selects credentials from the exact\\n  participant session/run instead of forwarding an operator bearer to public\\n  participant routes. Successful participant responses populate a separate,\\n  bounded owner/credential store; rotation replaces only the token, and a\\n  confirmed-logout tombstone preserves owners and pending answers while\\n  disabling local legacy fallback. Participant SSE and worker saves use the\\n  same credential selection. Worker credentials are delivery metadata only:\\n  answer bytes, request body, delivery ID and foreground outbox stay unchanged.\\n  Invalid metadata cannot discard a valid queued answer. Fourteen actual\\n  frontend/worker-state tests passed, along with a fresh protected SQLite/\\n  Chromium gate through Original/Rewrite entry, real Verona offline recovery\\n  and view-closure background delivery; the browser gate rejects operator-token\\n  forwarding. A headful check also passed Original footer/account keyboard\\n  behavior and same-run return. Successful HTTP sign-in and credential-based\\n  launch now issue a fresh participant token. Every known session/run HTTP\\n  operation requires its exact owner's credential; neither an operator token,\\n  foreign participant token, stable ID nor resource capability can bypass it.\\n  DELETE session access returns 205 after compare-and-revoke without deleting\\n  the session, run or responses. SSE access is rechecked on each poll and\\n  revocation closes an existing stream. A dedicated real HTTP test proves\\n  unauthorized reads/writes, preserved execution-mode restrictions, revoked\\n  resources/streams, stale-logout rejection and exact response restoration after\\n  re-login. The full API suites passed with memory, file and SQLite (161 per\\n  store); seventeen frontend/worker/test-actor tests passed. The PostgreSQL\\n  integration gate and all three Compose PostgreSQL smoke variants passed in\\n  the HTTP-ownership checkpoint's CI run. That run is not overall green:\\n  repeated Test Controller setup logins rotate credentials that the browser\\n  then incorrectly reuses. These fixtures are being corrected through real UI\\n1253:ui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-delete\\n1260:ui_smoke_step=nav-content\\n1261:ui_smoke_step=assemble-loose-original-source-files\\n1271:ui_smoke_step=resolve-loose-original-workspace-dependencies\\n1285:ui_smoke_step=resolve-ambiguous-workspace-dependency\\n M README.md\\n M apps/web/src/app/original-participant-account.component.ts\\n M apps/web/src/app/participant-access-credentials.ts\\n M apps/web/src/app/participant-view.facade.ts\\n M docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md\\n M docs/PARITY.md\\n M package.json\\n M scripts/participant-access-credentials.test.mjs\\n M scripts/smoke-ui.mjs\\n?? apps/web/src/app/participant-sign-out.ts\\n?? docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\\n?? scripts/participant-sign-out.test.mjs\\nd341434b Enforce participant ownership and revocation across HTTP channels\\nd208f383 Bind browser and background requests to participant credentials\\n8879f43c Separate player resource capabilities from participant access\\n15db665f Diagnose workspace refresh interactions in browser gates\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634","create_time":1791052686.907664}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
