er\ndocs/PARITY.md:128:  browser's credential store; existing keys and logout tombstones are never\ndocs/PARITY.md:132:  Original Starter logout waits for actual HTTP revocation before clearing the\ndocs/PARITY.md:137:  logout-state regressions passed. A headful Chromium/owned-SQLite check passed\ndocs/PARITY.md:138:  a real Player answer save, temporary logout failure and retry, old-key 401,\ndocs/PARITY.md:140:  the Player, desktop focus and mobile keyboard logout without overflow or\ndocs/PARITY.md:143:  browser gate passed through Original logout/re-entry, all official Player\ndocs/PARITY.md:192:An additional development-build run exposed `NG0100` in the Participant view\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\ndocs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md:112:byte-identical answer restoration, desktop focus and mobile keyboard logout.\ndocs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md:113:Twenty-five frontend/worker/test-actor/logout-state tests passed. The current\ndocs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md:116:passed through this logout/re-entry path, official Player and Test Controller\ndocs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md:119:this verifies the server-backed logout path, not the complete visual-parity\nREADME.md:846:open `Nutzerinformationen` and choose `Abmelden` to revoke participant access.\nREADME.md:850:participant is not cleared by a stale logout completion. Re-entry through real\ndocs/PARITY.md:57:  exposes the separately verified server-backed logout described below.\ndocs/PARITY.md:74:  Unit and memory/file/SQLite store regressions cover rotation, stale logout,\ndocs/PARITY.md:77:  and Original Starter account logout now use this service; local session\ndocs/PARITY.md:95:  confirmed-logout tombstone preserves owners and pending answers while\ndocs/PARITY.md:112:  resources/streams, stale-logout rejection and exact response restoration after\ndocs/PARITY.md:128:  browser's credential store; existing keys and logout tombstones are never\ndo